!! Q: Do I need the theme plugin if I only use one rimir plugin?

Yes, if that plugin uses `rr-` CSS classes (most do). Without theme, the UI will render but without proper styling — no borders, no spacing, no callout colors. Check the plugin's dependencies to confirm.

!! Q: Will theme conflict with my custom TW palette?

No. Theme uses TiddlyWiki's `<<colour ...>>` macros for most colors (borders, backgrounds, muted text), so it inherits your active palette automatically. Only semantic colors (callout borders, notice backgrounds) use hardcoded values.

!! Q: How do I override a specific `rr-` class?

Create a tiddler tagged `$:/tags/Stylesheet` with higher specificity or an `!important` rule. Since TW loads stylesheet tiddlers in alphabetical order by title, you can also use a title that sorts after the theme's `styles.tid` to ensure your overrides load later.

